  Let $(L,w)|(F,v)$ be a finite and purely inseparable extension of valued fields, such that $\mathrm{Char} F \neq \ell$.
  Then the canonical map $\operatorname{k}^{\rm M}_1(F) \rightarrow \operatorname{k}^{\rm M}_1(L)$ restricts to an isomorphism $\{{\rm U}_v\}_F \xrightarrow{\cong} \{{\rm U}_w\}_L$.

