  Then the following hold:
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item The restriction $\phi|_{\mathcal{U}_2} \in \mathrm{Aut}^{\rm c}(\pi^a|_{\mathcal{U}_2})$ is also defined by $\tau$. 
    \item If there exists some $\epsilon \in (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ and some $\tau' \in {\mathrm{Gal}_{k_0}}$ such that $\epsilon \cdot \phi|_{\mathcal{U}_2}$ is defined by $\tau'$, then $\tau' = \tau$ and $\epsilon = 1$.
  \end{enumerate}

